f 17592186382748 13194139536083 true] [17592186382747 1110 #uuid "18b2c6a1-89fb-570b-8112-700a06af6483" 13194139536083 true] [17592186382748 1034 "0" 13194139536083 true] [17592186382748 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536083 true] [17592186382748 1111 #uuid "3de1fde5-b622-518b-ad82-82149805110c" 13194139536083 true] [17592186382749 1017 #edb/ref 17592186382750 13194139536083 true] [17592186382749 1089 "q-336899" 13194139536083 true] [17592186382749 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536083 true] [17592186382749 1100 "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n$\\,{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{x}^{2}-2x+1}{({x}^{2}-9)^{2}+32x-96}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139536083 true] [17592186382749 1113 #uuid "7b1ee7cf-14c4-52ed-a4c9-8bd4dbb68e27" 13194139536083 true] [17592186382749 1145 "If we plug in $x=1$ we get the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ so  we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{x}^{2}-2x+1}{({x}^{2}-9)^{2}+32x-96} & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{[{x}^{2}-2x+1]}^{′}}{{[({x}^{2}-9)^{2}+32x-96]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{2x-2}{4x({x}^{2}-9)+32} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{x-1}{2{x}^{3}-18x+16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{x}^{2}-2x+1}{({x}^{2}-9)^{2}+32x-96} & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{x-1}{2{x}^{3}-18x+16} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{[x-1]}^{′}}{{[2{x}^{3}-18x+16]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{1}{6{x}^{2}-18} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6(1)^{2}-18} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536083 true] [17592186382750 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382751 13194139536083 true] [17592186382750 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536083 true] [17592186382750 1041 "field-1" 13194139536083 true] [17592186382750 1104 #edb/ref 17592186382751 13194139536083 true] [17592186382750 1110 #uuid "429278f0-2f1d-561f-b7b3-f0620da95645" 13194139536083 true] [17592186382751 1034 "-\\frac{1}{12}" 13194139536083 true] [17592186382751 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536083 true] [17592186382751 1111 #uuid "e7f9b1ad-6574-5f0a-98e2-03b07773efc8" 13194139536083 true] [17592186382752 1017 #edb/ref 17592186382753 13194139536083 true] [17592186382752 1089 "q-336939" 13194139536083 true] [17592186382752 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536083 true] [17592186382752 1100 "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n$\\,{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+5x)-5x}{{x}^{2}}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139536083 true] [17592186382752 1113 #uuid "f590b133-99f7-591b-b6c9-d85e4d4334e5" 13194139536083 true] [17592186382752 1145 "If we plug in $x=0$ we get the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ so  we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+5x)-5x}{{x}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+5x)-5x]}^{′}}{[{x}^{2}]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(\\frac{5}{1+5x}-5)}{2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(\\frac{1}{1+5x}-1)}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+5x)-5x}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{5}{2}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(\\frac{1}{1+5x}-1)}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{[(1+5x)^{-1}-1]}^{′}}{[x]^{′}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{lim}_{x\\to 0}(-5(1+5x)^{-2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}(-5) \\\\  & =-\\frac{25}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536083 true] [17592186382753 1000 #edb/ref 17592186382754 13194139536083 true] [17592186382753 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536083 true] [17592186382753 1041 "field-1" 13194139536083 true] [17592186382753 1104 #edb/ref 17592186382754 13194139536083 true] [17592186382753 1110 #uuid "cc93b39c-eb23-566a-930e-a415dee59caf" 13194139536083 true] [17592186382754 1034 "-\\frac{25}{2}" 13194139536083 true] [1759